 county&rsquo;s 4 grids June to July came in under 90% of normal in 35 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 72% of normal in June to July, 64% in July to August and 53% in August to September. This year so far, May to June 2026 came in at 151%, and the preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 on grid 29628 sits at 75.0.</p>"}
